## Understanding Linux File Permissions

### Permission String Example
```text
drwxr-x--- bob bob
```

| Component | Meaning |
| :--- | :--- |
| **d** | File type indicator (**d**irectory) |
| **rwx** | Owner permissions (read, write, execute) |
| **r-x** | Group permissions (read, execute, no write) |
| **---** | Others/World permissions (no access) |
| **bob** (1st) | Account owner of the directory |
| **bob** (2nd) | Group owner associated with the directory |
